class Solution {
public:
    int hammingWeight(uint32_t n) {
        int count = 0;

        while (n != 0) {
            n = n & (n - 1);
            count++;
        }

        return count;
    }
};

Intuition: n & (n - 1) removes the rightmost 1 bit.
Algorithm: Repeat this operation and count how many times it can be performed.
Key Idea: Each iteration removes exactly one set bit.
Time Complexity: O(k), where k is the number of 1 bits.
Space Complexity: O(1).
